        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-10T21:40:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The headerKeyValuePairs is needed to retrieve a unique payload ID of the payload (see applyPayload). Similar to applyPayload, this function needs to detect duplicate calls with the same payload (which should do nothing, similar to \"resume\" in applyPayload) and multiple calls with different payloads (which should free up space used by previous payload and re-allocate).\n\nPlease see the update_engine CL as well for the implementation of this function.",
      "parentUuid": "c64d8512_b43f4e14",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 435,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 439,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "3d0103098dc33b84aed922f0e410cfa1435aaba0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "432ee6f4_e0161be8",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/UpdateEngine.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 439,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-10T21:42:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Especially, in the \"duplicate calls with the same payload\" case, since the update may be resuming, the allocated space must NOT be freed then reallocated; otherwise, the previous progress is lost.",
